 "notes": "All four old kinds kept with old sources; Elm & zelkova, Satsuki, Flowering & fruiting and Kokedama added from Wikipedia. Old 'Itoigawa' and 'Kyushu' became versions of Shimpaku; old Pinus pentaphylla merged into Japanese white pine. Styles and size classes as t types (size classes as named on the Wikipedia Bonsai page; 'chuhin' not on any retrieved page so 'chumono' used). Left out for lack of a retrieved page: 'Kishu' juniper, crabapple bonsai, Shunka-en nursery as a brand (Kunio Kobayashi page names only the Shunkaen Bonsai Museum, listed under the Japanese bonsai tradition). No brand entries: no archetype has a maker."
